    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: # PHP Login Form Guide
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Introduction
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: In this guide, we will create a simple PHP login form. This form will capture user details such as username and password. We will also discuss secure coding practices and how to implement the form effectively.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Creating the Login Form
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: To create a basic login form in PHP, you can use the following example:
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ### Example Code
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ```php
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <!DOCTYPE html>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <html lang="de">
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <head>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <title>Login</title>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: </head>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <body>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <h2>Bitte melde dich an!</h2>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <form method="post" action="login.php">
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <input type="text" name="username" placeholder="Benutzername" required>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <input type="password" name="password" placeholder="Passwort" required>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: <button type="submit">Anmelden</button>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: </form>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: </body>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: </html>
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ```
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ### Explanation of Code Parts
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - **`<!DOCTYPE html>`**: Indicates that the file is an HTML document.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - **`<title>`**: Sets the title of the page.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - **`<h2>`**: Creates a title for the form.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - **`<form method="post">`**: Defines the form and specifies that data will be sent using the POST method.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - **`<input type="text">`**: Creates a text input field for the username.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - **`<input type="password">`**: Creates a password input field.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - **`<button type="submit">`**: Creates a submit button for the form.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Important Considerations
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 1. **Security**:
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Use secure coding practices, such as validating and sanitizing user input.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Consider using HTTPS to protect user data during transmission.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 2. **Styling**:
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - You can apply CSS to style the form and improve its appearance.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 3. **Testing**:
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - Test the form thoroughly to ensure it works as expected.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: 4. **Integration**:
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: - You can integrate this form into a WordPress plugin or other applications as needed.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: ## Conclusion
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: This guide provides a basic overview of creating a PHP login form. You can expand upon this foundation by adding features such as user registration, password recovery, and more advanced security measures.
    PACK-ES-IN-JIRA ORIGINAL: Feel free to reach out if you have any questions or need further assistance!
